            <title>[LU-21170] sanity-lnet test_156: expected export contains a peer learned before the export, not in actual</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21170</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;sanity-lnet test_156 (import of ip2nets with comma-separated IP ranges) compares a full "lnetctl export --backup" taken after add_net (expected) with an export after reinit_dlc and import (actual). It failed once on lustre-reviews review-ldiskfs-arm (aarch64) with "test_156 failed with 1":&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2806adaa-db64-465b-a375-4c011d0987aa" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/2806adaa-db64-465b-a375-4c011d0987aa&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The expected export contains a peer that the actual export lacks:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  peer:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;primary nid: 10.240.29.33@tcp&lt;br/&gt;
        Multi-Rail: true&lt;br/&gt;
        peer ni:&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;nid: 10.240.29.33@tcp&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;The node under test is 10.240.29.35 and the import file lists only 10.240.29.&lt;span class="error"&gt;&amp;#91;37,39,35,41,43&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;, so a peer for .33 is not configured by the test. It was learned (a message or discovery from another node of the cluster) in the window between add_net and the expected export, and it cannot reappear after reinit_dlc. The comparison is therefore racy when any other node sends to the test node at that point. The diff is only in the peer section; net and global sections are identical.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Rate: about 1 in 6900 runs on review-ldiskfs-arm over 400 days (no other failure of this type found; the other test_156 failures in that period are module-unload, rc = 234 and network-loss errors). It was seen on change 70374 (lnet response tracker patch), which does not create peers; the other 3 runs of the group on that change and 1511 other review runs in 30 days passed.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possible fix: have the test export only the net and global sections, or filter out peers not created by the test, or run "lnetctl peer del" / disable discovery before taking the expected export.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-70374-ps2-ef9594de7612 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/70374" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/70374&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
